  "result": "Fixed. The quote now prints 27.06 and all 6 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py:9` right-padded the fractional part with zeros. A one-digit fraction like the \"5\" in \"12.5\" became \"05\", so the price parsed as 12.05 instead of 12.50. Two units at 12.05 plus 8.25% tax gave 26.09.\n\n**Fix:** pad on the right instead, so \"5\" becomes \"50\". Prices with two decimals were unaffected, which is why the existing tests never caught it.\n\n**Tests:** pytest is not installed, so I ran the suite with unittest discovery. All 6 tests pass. None of them cover one-decimal input, so adding a `to_cents(\"12.5\") == 1250` case to `tests/test_pricing.py` would guard against a regression.",
